@startuml
title OaK architecture: four main interfaces

top to bottom direction
hide stereotype
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

skinparam package<<agent>> {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7DF
  BorderColor #B45F06
  FontColor #7A4A00
}

skinparam rectangle<<module>> {
  BackgroundColor #FFE599
  BorderColor #B45F06
  FontColor #5F3B00
  FontStyle bold
}

skinparam artifact {
  BackgroundColor #F3F3F3
  BorderColor #999999
  FontColor #333333
}

actor caller

artifact time_step
artifact "step memory\nlast_subjective_state\nlast_action" as step_memory
artifact subjective_state
artifact "transition\n(internal step record)" as transition
artifact planning_update
artifact action

package "OaKAgent\n(default interface layer)" <<agent>> {
  rectangle "Perception" as perception <<module>>
  rectangle "TransitionModel" as transition_model <<module>>
  rectangle "ValueFunction" as value_function <<module>>
  rectangle "ReactivePolicy" as reactive_policy <<module>>

  perception -[hidden]right-> transition_model
  perception -[hidden]down-> value_function
  transition_model -[hidden]down-> reactive_policy
  value_function -[hidden]right-> reactive_policy
}

caller -up-> time_step
time_step --> perception : perceive(...)
perception --> subjective_state : current state estimate

step_memory --> transition : previous state + action
time_step --> transition : reward, terminated,\ninfo
subjective_state --> transition : next subjective state
transition --> value_function : learn from transition
transition --> transition_model : learn model / options
transition --> reactive_policy : learn policy / options

subjective_state --> transition_model : planning start state
value_function --> transition_model : value predictions
transition_model --> planning_update : plan result
planning_update --> reactive_policy : planning advice

subjective_state --> reactive_policy : decision context
reactive_policy --> action : primitive action
action -down-> caller : AgentStepResult.action

note right of transition
Built inside OaKAgent.step(...)
only when a previous state/action exists.
end note

note bottom
This is the default conceptual surface of OaK:
OaKAgent coordinates four main interfaces.
It shows the four slots and the main data flow, not every method.
For the fine-grained interface inventory, see oak_architecture.
end note

@enduml
